Obviously everyone has their own strengths and weaknesses, but I can
relate to Rachel's comment that making a big mistake really wakes me
up.  Most of my nethack ascensions are less than 30k turns and I tend
to make really stupid errors about once every 10k-30k turns so I tend
to only need one amulet.  I find Nethack to be at times mentally
taxing and thus by the end of a game I am far more prone to make a
mistake.  And there are always new ways to die!

The other piece about the AoLS that I like is that it allows me to
play much more cavalierly and quickly during the endgame, by which
time I am ready to ascend and start a new game or possibly trying to
ascend in record time.  Famine or Pestilence is guarding the altar? So
what? Just jump past him and if he kills me it's fine, I won't even
lose a turn!  But even still by combining sickness, stunning, ill, and/
or blind attacks the residents of the planes can still kill a hero
even with herculean build.





